{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nprimes = []\r\nfor p in range(2, 6000):\r\n    is_prime = True\r\n    for p2 in primes:\r\n        if p2*p2 > p:\r\n            break\r\n        if p % p2==0:\r\n            is_prime = False\r\n            break\r\n    if is_prime:\r\n        primes.append(p)\r\n        \r\ndef factor(n):\r\n    d = {}\r\n    for p in primes:\r\n        if p*p > n:\r\n            break\r\n        if n % p==0:\r\n            c = 0\r\n            while n % p==0:\r\n                n = n//p\r\n                c+=1\r\n            d[p] = c\r\n    if n > 1:\r\n        d[n] = 1\r\n    return d\r\n\r\ndef factors(n):\r\n    d = factor(n)\r\n    answer = [1]\r\n    for p in d:\r\n        a2 = []\r\n        for x in answer:\r\n            for i in range(d[p]+1):\r\n                a2.append(x*p**i)\r\n        answer = a2\r\n    return answer\r\n        \r\n\r\ndef process(n, m):\r\n    f_dict = {0: 0, 1: 1, 2: 2}\r\n    for i in range(3, n+1):\r\n        f_dict[i] = 2*f_dict[i-1]\r\n        for x in factors(i):\r\n            if 2 <= x <= i:\r\n                f_dict[i] += f_dict[(i//x)]-f_dict[(i-1)//x]\r\n                f_dict[i] = f_dict[i] % m\r\n        f_dict[i] = f_dict[i] % m\r\n    return f_dict[n]\r\n\r\nn, m = [int(x) for x in input().split()]\r\nprint(process(n, m))\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <map>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nvector<int> primes;\n\nvoid generate_primes() {\n    for (int p = 2; p < 6000; ++p) {\n        bool is_prime = true;\n        for (int p2 : primes) {\n            if (p2 * p2 > p) break;\n            if (p % p2 == 0) {\n                is_prime = false;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n        if (is_prime) primes.push_back(p);\n    }\n}\n\nmap<int, int> factor(int n) {\n    map<int, int> d;\n    for (int p : primes) {\n        if (p * p > n) break;\n        if (n % p == 0) {\n            int c = 0;\n            while (n % p == 0) {\n                n /= p;\n                ++c;\n            }\n            d[p] = c;\n        }\n    }\n    if (n > 1) d[n] = 1;\n    return d;\n}\n\nvector<long long> factors(int n) {\n    map<int, int> d = factor(n);\n    vector<long long> answer = {1};\n    for (auto &entry : d) {\n        int p = entry.first;\n        int e = entry.second;\n        vector<long long> a2;\n        for (long long x : answer) {\n            long long mult = 1;\n            for (int i = 0; i <= e; ++i) {\n                a2.push_back(x * mult);\n                mult *= p;\n            }\n        }\n        answer = a2;\n    }\n    return answer;\n}\n\nlong long process(int n, long long m) {\n    if (n == 0) return 0;\n    if (n == 1) return 1 % m;\n    if (n == 2) return 2 % m;\n    vector<long long> f(n + 1);\n    f[0] = 0;\n    f[1] = 1 % m;\n    f[2] = 2 % m;\n    for (int i = 3; i <= n; ++i) {\n        f[i] = (2 * f[i - 1]) % m;\n        vector<long long> divs = factors(i);\n        for (long long x : divs) {\n            if (x >= 2 && x <= i) {\n                long long diff = f[i / x] - f[(i - 1) / x];\n                diff = (diff % m + m) % m;\n                f[i] = (f[i] + diff) % m;\n            }\n        }\n        f[i] %= m;\n    }\n    return f[n];\n}\n\nint main() {\n    generate_primes();\n    int n;\n    long long m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n    cout << process(n, m) << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -0.00013183678674977273, -0.00037317464011721313, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.000262106885202229, -1.2993727978027891e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.7881377516459906e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -4.6967357775429264e-05, -0.0003369478799868375, -4.541770613286644e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0806848406791687, -0.12697340548038483, -0.014164037071168423, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.011052104644477367, -0.06200089305639267, -0.01110044214874506, -2.622600959512056e-06, 0.0, -0.005237548612058163, -0.6341024041175842, -0.008614521473646164, 0.0, -0.011461484245955944, -0.0056531080044806, -0.10022103041410446, -0.1516045778989792, -0.023248940706253052, 0.0, -0.12723837792873383, -4.768370445162873e-07, -4.410734163684538e-06, -0.054921574890613556, -1.2993727978027891e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -8.4638240878121e-06, -1.2993727978027891e-05, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0007179781678132713, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.5497195136049413e-06, 0.0, -0.008614994585514069, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -2.0265558760002023e-06, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, -8.511180931236595e-05, -5.364274329622276e-05, 0.0, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -5.483612312673358e-06, 0.0, -0.014274394139647484, -0.00011657988943625242, 0.0, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.311301275563892e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00043084874050691724, 0.